00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:19.120
When D'Angelo is saying, and Toby, you're getting a new chair, whether he likes it or not.
当迪安杰洛说：“还有托比，你要换把新椅子，不管他喜不喜欢。”

159
00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.720
Toby says, thanks.
托比说：“谢谢。”

160
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.260
And D'Angelo says, don't thank me.
然后迪安杰洛说：“别谢我。”

161
00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.140
Hey, don't thank me, guy.
嘿，别谢我，伙计。

162
00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.000
That wasn't in the script.
那句台词剧本里没有。

163
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.260
And you can see Craig's like shoulders like shaking.
你可以看到克雷格的肩膀在抖。

164
00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:36.020
I mean, we should say that Will like would improvise here and there and we would all lose it.
我是说，我们得提一下，威尔偶尔会即兴发挥，然后我们所有人都会笑喷。

165
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.140
Will can read the phone book and be funny.
威尔就算念电话簿都能念得很有趣。

166
00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.800
I mean, every line he says is funny.
我是说，他说的每一句台词都很好笑。

167
00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.280
All right.
好吧。

168
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.040
So now the episode begins.
那么现在剧集开始了。

169
00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:55.180
D'Angelo and Daryl are arriving to work and Pam is going to interrupt their chat to tell him about her friend Carla, who might make a great executive assistant.
迪安杰洛和达里尔到达公司，帕姆打断了他们的谈话，想告诉他关于她朋友卡拉的事，她可能是一个很棒的行政助理。

170
00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:04.840
I remember that the NBC photographer was here this day when we were shooting this and they took pictures of this scene and I charged them.
我记得拍这一天的时候NBC的摄影师在现场，他们拍了这一幕，我还向他们收费了。

171
00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:05.880
I bet.
我敢打赌。

172
00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.860
Well, you know, Pam's runner with the resumes was bigger.
嗯，你知道的，帕姆关于简历的那个小插曲其实更长。

173
00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.620
There's more of it in deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有更多内容。

174
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:12.800
I'm going to share some of it.
我打算分享一些。

175
00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:20.980
But one of the things that tickled me, Jenna, is I'm such a nerd for this, for whatever character gets to say the title of a movie or an episode.
但有一件事让我觉得很有趣，珍娜，我在这方面是个书呆子，不管哪个角色能说出电影或剧集的标题，我都很兴奋。

176
00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.420
I just think it's so cool.
我就是觉得这太酷了。

177
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.200
And Pam gets to say the title of this episode.
而且帕姆说出了这一集的标题。

178
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:25.740
Really?
真的吗？

179
00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.260
Yeah.
是的。

180
00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:30.880
She says to Jim, oh, is that what he says in your little inner circle meetings?
她对吉姆说：“噢，这就是他在你们那个所谓的小圈子会议上说的话吗？”

181
00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.020
Oh, yes, you're right.
噢，是的，你说得对。

182
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.600
I was like, ah, she said the title.
我当时就想，啊，她说出标题了。

183
00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.880
I'm a dork for stuff like that.
我对这种事就是个呆子。

184
00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:36.440
You point it out every time.
你每次都会指出来。

185
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:36.780
I know.
我知道。

186
00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.300
It's very cute.
这很可爱。

187
00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:37.660
Okay.
好的。

188
00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.640
We got a fan catch from Aiden W.
我们收到了来自俄勒冈州波特兰市艾登·W的粉丝发现。

189
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.900
in Portland, Oregon, who said, there are three Carlas in the office.
他说，办公室里有三个叫卡拉的人。

190
00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:53.280
There is Carla, the mission trip leader, Carla, Pam's executive assistant friend, and coming up, Carla Fern, Andy's agent.
有传教旅行领队卡拉，帕姆的行政助理朋友卡拉，还有后面会出现的安迪的经纪人卡拉·费恩。

191
00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.300
What are the writers' obsession with the name Carla?
编剧们对“卡拉”这个名字是有什么执念吗？

192
00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.940
I've personally never met a Carla in my life.
我这辈子还没见过叫卡拉的人呢。

193
00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:00.220
Wow.
哇。

194
00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.820
I didn't realize there were three.
我没意识到竟然有三个。

195
00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.440
Yeah, three Carlas.
是啊，三个卡拉。

196
00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.780
That's such a great catch.
真是个了不起的发现。

197
00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.040
Andy and Pam are convinced there's an inner circle.
安迪和帕姆确信存在一个小圈子。

198
00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.640
Jim's like, no, there's no inner circle.
吉姆说：“不，没有小圈子。”

199
00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.060
And Kevin's like, he only says that because he's in it.
凯文说：“他这么说只是因为他就在圈子里。”

200
00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.360
And then Kevin is so proud.
然后凯文感到非常自豪。

201
00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.940
He's like, mom, I'm in the inner circle.
他说，妈，我可是核心圈子里的人。

202
00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.920
I loved that Kevin was in the inner circle.
我喜欢凯文身处核心圈子的设定。

203
00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.140
It was such a nice twiSt.
这真是一个很棒的反转。

204
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:21.560
Unexpected.
出人意料。

205
00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.200
Someone who is not in the inner circle or who doesn't want to be in the inner circle.
那些不在核心圈子里，或者不想进入核心圈子的人。

206
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.180
And D'Angelo is doing everything he can to get Dwight on his good side.
迪安杰洛正竭尽全力想讨好德怀特。

207
00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.360
He tries to bring him a coffee from downstairs.
他试着从楼下给德怀特带杯咖啡。

208
00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.920
Dwight throws it in the trash.
德怀特直接扔进了垃圾桶。

209
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:34.920
Not interested.
没兴趣。

210
00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:35.920
Not interested.
没兴趣。

211
00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:44.620
As soon as D'Angelo tries to entice Dwight with like some beers, and he said they can listen to Automatic for the People on his jukebox.
迪安杰洛刚试着用几瓶啤酒诱惑德怀特，还说他们可以在他的自动点唱机上听《Automatic for the People》这张专辑。

212
00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:53.280
Lady, I could not stop laughing because I have a little bit of backstory about the album Automatic for the People.
天哪，我当时笑得停不下来，因为我对《Automatic for the People》这张专辑有一点背景故事。

213
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:54.480
What?
什么？

214
00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:55.280
Okay.
好吧。

215
00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.080
I don't know this album.
我不知道这张专辑。

216
00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.040
Who sings this album?
是谁唱的？

217
00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:58.420
Oh, my God.
天哪。

218
00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.200
It's R.E.M.
是R.E.M.乐队。

219
00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.220
You do know this album.
你肯定知道这张专辑。

220
00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:00.640
You do.
你绝对知道。

221
00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.420
I promise you.
我向你保证。

222
00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:01.680
Okay.
好吧。

223
00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.000
Okay.
好吧。

224
00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:06.600
So it came out while I was in college in October 1992.
它是在1992年10月我上大学时发行的。

225
00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.740
You guys, I know I'm a dinosaur.
伙计们，我知道我是个老古董了。

226
00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.820
But when it came out, I was going through a breakup.
但它发行的时候，我刚好经历了一场分手。

227
00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:19.680
And I'm sorry I laughed, but I just like I know these moments where like, oh, this was your breakup album.
抱歉我笑了，但我就是觉得，我懂那种感觉，哦，原来这是你的分手专属专辑。

228
00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.100
Yes.
没错。

229
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.100
Did you listen to it just so much?
你当时是不是听了特别多遍？

230
00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.660
Oh, there was one song that instantly takes me back to that time.
哦，有一首歌能瞬间把我带回那个时候。

231
00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:26.860
It starts with this piano.
它以钢琴声开场。

232
00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.100
The song is called Night Swimming.
那首歌叫《Night Swimming》。

233
00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.500
I need you to hear a little bit of it.
我得让你听听看。

234
00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:34.780
And then I am going to read you an entry from my journal during this breakup.
然后我要给你读一段我分手期间写的日记。

235
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.140
You have made my day.
你真是让我今天过得太开心了。

236
00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:58.880
Okay.
好吧。

237
00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.240
Okay.
好吧。

238
00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.320
You're getting the idea right.
你明白我的意思了，对吧。

239
00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:01.120
I'm in a mood.
我很有感触。

240
00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.140
You're in a mood.
你很有感触。

241
00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:02.900
I'm feeling it.
我感受到了。

242
00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.540
Now I'm almost curled up in a ball.
我现在整个人都快缩成一团了。

243
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.020
Okay.
好吧。

244
00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.120
Now I'm opening my journal.
我现在要打开我的日记了。

245
00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:07.740
Okay.
好吧。

246
00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:08.160
Here we go.
开始了。

247
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.220
It's super old.
这本子超级旧了。

248
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:15.600
First of all, you guys should know, I hadn't been dating this guy very long, so I wasn't like super heartbroken.
首先，你们得知道，我和那个男生交往没多久，所以我并没有特别心碎。

249
00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.280
I was more just really ticked off.
我更多的是感到非常恼火。

250
00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:17.860
Okay.
好吧。

251
00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:18.260
Okay.
好吧。

252
00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:18.700
Okay.
好吧。

253
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.480
So, picture me listening to Night Swimming.
想象一下，我正在听《Night Swimming》这首歌。

254
00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.480
I'm ticked off.
我气坏了。

255
00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.580
Here we go.
开始了。

256
00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.200
October 17th, 1992.
1992年10月17日。

257
00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:28.040
Okay.
好吧。

258
00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:29.840
Come on.
拜托。

259
00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:32.540
Okay.
好吧。

260
00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:38.880
I know I said that I wasn't going to talk about him anymore, but he has stooped too far.
我知道我说过不再提他了，但他这次做得太过分了。

261
00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:44.480
He is a lying snake, a shell of a man, and a liar.
他是个撒谎的毒蛇，是个空壳男人，是个骗子。

262
00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.380
He is hanging out with his ex-girlfriend.
他竟然和他的前女友混在一起。

263
00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.940
He has done nothing but lie.
他除了撒谎什么都没干。

264
00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:54.220
It is going to take all that I have to be cordial to him.
我得使出浑身解数才能对他保持客气。

265
00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.140
Oh, boy.
天哪。

266
00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.960
He disgusts me.
他真让我恶心。

267
00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:59.780
I need to broaden my horizons.
我得开阔一下眼界了。

268
00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.200
What do I care?
我管他呢？

269
00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.060
This is all so trivial.
这一切都太琐碎了。

270
00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:12.400
I have a wonderfully attractive life ahead of me, and I am grateful that Mr. Self-Centered isn't a part of it.
我未来的人生精彩纷呈，我很庆幸那个“自我中心先生”不再是其中的一部分了。

271
00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.100
Amen.
阿门。

272
00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:14.900
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

273
00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.480
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

274
00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:20.760
Am I the dorkiest person ever?
我是有史以来最呆的人吗？

275
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.000
It's going to take all I have to be cordial to him.
我得使出浑身解数才能对他保持客气。

276
00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:28.820
Lady, I need you to write like a young adult novel series.
女士，我需要你写一套青少年小说系列。

277
00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:32.320
This one is called Mr. Self-Centered.
这一本叫《自我中心先生》。

278
00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.720
Then you've got another one called Mr. Maybe.
然后你还有另一本叫《也许先生》。

279
00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.280
So we, do you know what I'm saying?
所以我们，你明白我的意思吗？

280
00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:37.600
Yes.
明白。

281
00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:45.520
It's a series of just the dating foibles of this young woman who is taking her power back.
这是一个系列，讲述了一个年轻女性在夺回生活主导权过程中的约会糗事。

282
00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.460
I didn't even tell him off.
我甚至都没骂他。

283
00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.440
Like, I just, I was cordial.
我只是，我表现得很客气。

284
00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:51.700
Take that.
受着吧。

285
00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.920
But I'm going to be not friendly to you.
但我以后不会再对你友好了。

286
00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:56.220
Yeah.
没错。

287
00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.480
All you get from me, mister, is cordial.
先生，你从我这儿得到的只会是客气。

288
00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.160
That's right.
没错。

289
00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.160
And maybe a snarky look.
可能还会有一个讽刺的眼神。

290
00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.100
Well, you showed him.
好吧，你让他见识到了。

291
00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.240
Well, there was a moment from my journal.
好吧，那是我日记里的一段记录。

292
00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:07.640
I hope you guys enjoyed it.
希望你们喜欢。

293
00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.600
What's the end of this story?
这个故事的结局是什么？

294
00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:10.880
Did you ever run into him?
你后来还遇到过他吗？

295
00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:11.800
Were you cordial?
你对他客气了吗？

296
00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:12.520
Yeah.
遇到了。

297
00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:16.280
I had to run into him all the time, and I was cordial and a bit dismissive.
我不得不经常见到他，我表现得很客气，还有点不屑一顾。

298
00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

299
00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:24.940
So don't mess with me, because you're going to get someone who's maybe a little bored,
所以别惹我，因为你面对的将是一个可能有点无聊，

300
00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:25.660
but polite.
但很有礼貌的人。

301
00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:26.660
Yeah.
没错。

302
00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.180
One other thing happening in this scene.
这一幕里还有另一件事。

303
00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.920
Three minutes, 56 seconds.
三分56秒。

304
00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.120
Aunt Farm still on Dwight's desk.
“蚂蚁农场”还在德怀特的桌子上。

305
00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.700
I appreciate the commitment to a prop.
我很欣赏这种对道具的执着。

306
00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:37.400
I know.
我知道。

307
00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:37.800
Me too.
我也是。

308
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.680
D'Angelo is going to say, try as he may.
迪安杰洛会说，尽管他努力尝试。

309
00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.520
Dwight just wants nothing to do with him.
德怀特就是不想跟他有任何瓜葛。

310
00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.300
You know, after D'Angelo's talking head, Dwight would have had one.
你知道吗，在迪安杰洛的采访镜头之后，德怀特本该也有一个的。

311
00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.000
There was one in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里本来有一个。

312
00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.980
There was also some candy bag alts for it.
当时还有一些关于糖果袋的备选台词。

313
00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.400
I want to read one of them, because it really cracked me up.
我想读其中一个，因为它真的让我笑喷了。

314
00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.280
Because I can hear Rain saying it as Dwight.
因为我能听到雷恩用德怀特的口吻说出来。

315
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.000
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

316
00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.360
Here it is.
就是这个。

317
00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:02.860
D'Angelo is a fine manager, but I don't do my job for the approval of my employer.
迪安杰洛是个不错的经理，但我工作不是为了得到雇主的认可。

318
00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.920
I do it because if I didn't do it, some idiot would be doing it.
我工作是因为如果我不做，就会有某个白痴来做。

319
00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.640
And this way, that idiot is out of a job.
这样一来，那个白痴就没工作了。

320
00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.000
Ha ha, idiot.
