不，因为……

811
00:33:47.100 --> 00:33:48.400
I'm just going to keep saying that.
我打算一直这么说。

812
00:33:48.400 --> 00:33:49.100
It was...
当时……

813
00:33:49.100 --> 00:33:51.520
No, it was like, you know...
不，就像是，你知道的……

814
00:33:52.240 --> 00:33:53.460
Long distance is hard.
异地恋很难。

815
00:33:53.460 --> 00:33:55.480
We didn't break up right at that trip.
我们并不是在那次旅行时就分手的。

816
00:33:55.720 --> 00:33:55.880
Sure.
当然。

817
00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:58.420
But it was, you know, it was the beginning of the end.
但你知道，那是分手的开始。

818
00:33:58.600 --> 00:33:58.740
Right.
没错。

819
00:33:59.080 --> 00:34:02.520
You know, it was going to become clear that we were going in two different directions.
你知道，很明显我们正走向两个不同的方向。

820
00:34:02.860 --> 00:34:02.960
Right.
没错。

821
00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:05.480
And it wasn't the direction where we both juggle.
而且那不是我们俩都能一起抛球的方向。

822
00:34:05.880 --> 00:34:06.040
Yeah.
是啊。

823
00:34:06.200 --> 00:34:12.240
He was going to be a juggler and I was going to be an actor and not juggle.
他要成为一名抛球杂耍者，而我要成为一名演员，不去抛球。

824
00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.020
I feel like there's a world where you two could have made it.
我觉得你们俩本来是有可能在一起的。

825
00:34:16.140 --> 00:34:18.160
It should be like a traveling show.
那应该像个巡回演出一样。

826
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:22.420
You would come out, you would do your clown work.
你出场，表演你的小丑戏。

827
00:34:22.660 --> 00:34:23.880
He's a doctor now.
他现在是个医生了。

828
00:34:23.960 --> 00:34:24.400
Oh!
噢！

829
00:34:24.700 --> 00:34:24.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

830
00:34:25.520 --> 00:34:25.960
So...
所以……

831
00:34:25.960 --> 00:34:27.340
Well, that went a different way.
好吧，事情走向了另一个方向。

832
00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:27.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

833
00:34:28.820 --> 00:34:31.340
Listen, I find juggling cool.
听着，我觉得抛球很酷。

834
00:34:31.340 --> 00:34:32.440
I think it's neat.
我觉得这很棒。

835
00:34:32.880 --> 00:34:33.580
I do.
真的。

836
00:34:33.900 --> 00:34:38.940
So, you know, I was being real with him when I said I thought it was cool that he could juggle.
所以，你知道，当我说我觉得他会抛球很酷时，我是真心的。

837
00:34:38.940 --> 00:34:43.460
And I kind of still do wish I could juggle, but it clearly was not meant to be.
我其实还是希望自己能学会抛球，但显然这注定是不可能的。

838
00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:45.600
Wasn't meant to be, lady.
注定是不可能的，女士。

839
00:34:45.840 --> 00:34:46.100
No.
不。

840
00:34:46.980 --> 00:34:47.440
Okay.
好吧。

841
00:34:47.860 --> 00:34:48.900
Well, where are we?
那么，我们讲到哪了？

842
00:34:49.300 --> 00:34:52.760
We are at Jim asking for a moment of D'Angelo's time.
讲到吉姆请求占用迪安杰洛一点时间。

843
00:34:53.100 --> 00:34:55.200
And he has plenty of it because you know what?
而且他有的是时间，因为你知道吗？

844
00:34:55.280 --> 00:34:56.160
This job's a joke.
这份工作简直是个笑话。

845
00:34:56.540 --> 00:34:57.520
I loved that line.
我很喜欢那句台词。

846
00:34:57.540 --> 00:34:58.240
I loved it too.
我也很喜欢。

847
00:34:58.840 --> 00:35:04.180
I want to give a shout out to John Krasinski because the way he goes about bringing up
我要给约翰·卡拉辛斯基点个赞，因为他提出

848
00:35:04.180 --> 00:35:09.220
the women are unhappy and then just trying to backpedal and then all of it.
女员工们很不满，然后又试图退缩，以及整个过程的处理方式。

849
00:35:09.340 --> 00:35:11.960
He is so good in this scene.
他在这一幕里演得太好了。

850
00:35:12.560 --> 00:35:15.720
But then Jim kind of throws Pam under the bus.
但随后吉姆有点把帕姆给出卖了。

851
00:35:15.860 --> 00:35:21.540
Like what Pam and these women needed from Jim is for Jim to be an upstander.
帕姆和这些女同事真正需要吉姆做的是站出来主持公道。

852
00:35:21.660 --> 00:35:26.820
They needed him to go in the office and say, I've noticed that you do this thing.
她们需要他走进办公室说：我注意到你做了这件事。

853
00:35:26.940 --> 00:35:27.540
Let me point out.
让我指出来。

854
00:35:27.680 --> 00:35:28.760
But he doesn't do that.
但他并没有这样做。

855
00:35:28.940 --> 00:35:32.680
What he says is, so Angela, that's how he starts it off.
他开口说的是：安吉拉，他就是这样开头的。

856
00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:33.660
Oh, that's what I mean.
哦，我就是这个意思。

857
00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:37.160
Kevin brings up Pam and then says she can be kind of a bitch.
凯文提到了帕姆，然后说她有时候有点婊里婊气的。

858
00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:38.180
I know.
我知道。

859
00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:42.140
And Jim completely is like, blah, blah, blah, and then backs out.
而吉姆完全是一副“巴拉巴拉”的态度，然后就退缩了。

860
00:35:42.300 --> 00:35:43.080
Because he did it wrong.
因为他做错了。

861
00:35:43.300 --> 00:35:47.820
You're supposed to use your status and privilege and own what you're saying.
你应该利用你的地位和特权，并为你所说的话负责。

862
00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:54.420
You're not supposed to lay it off on the people who are experiencing the sexism, right?
你不应该把这种压力推给那些正在遭受性别歧视的人，对吧？

863
00:35:54.620 --> 00:35:58.460
You're like, I've noticed, D'Angelo, that there are no women in this room.
你应该说：迪安杰洛，我注意到这个房间里没有女性。

864
00:35:59.000 --> 00:36:02.820
I've noticed that Angela is a department head and you don't meet with her.
我注意到安吉拉是部门主管，但你从不跟她开会。

865
00:36:02.980 --> 00:36:05.400
And I think that that is somewhat of an issue.
我觉得这多少是个问题。

866
00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:07.220
So Jim tries.
所以吉姆尝试了。

867
00:36:07.240 --> 00:36:08.100
He tries.
他尝试了。

868
00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:11.060
But, you know, just have to say that.
但是，你知道，就是得把话说明白。

869
00:36:11.540 --> 00:36:12.200
I guess.
我想是吧。

870
00:36:12.360 --> 00:36:13.220
I guess I had to say that.
我想我必须得说出来。

871
00:36:13.300 --> 00:36:14.440
I have a lot of things to say today.
我今天有很多话要说。

872
00:36:14.580 --> 00:36:15.720
And by the way, I'm not done.
顺便说一句，我还没说完呢。

873
00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:17.660
I've got something to say about Phyllis in a minute.
待会儿我还有关于菲利斯的话要说。

874
00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:18.800
Oh, OK.
哦，好吧。

875
00:36:19.600 --> 00:36:22.360
Well, D'Angelo is now going to confront the bullpen.
好了，迪安杰洛现在要去找大办公室的人对质了。

876
00:36:22.620 --> 00:36:26.680
He's going to say, hey, I'm not a sexist, despite the rumor going around.
他要说：嘿，尽管有传言，但我不是性别歧视者。

877
00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:30.340
I do have a solitaire catch, 12 minutes, 14 seconds.
我玩纸牌接龙的纪录是12分14秒。

878
00:36:30.460 --> 00:36:31.000
I saw it.
我看到了。

879
00:36:31.380 --> 00:36:33.900
Kate Flannery is moving some cards around there in the background.
凯特·弗兰纳里在背景里挪动了一些牌。

880
00:36:34.360 --> 00:36:34.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

881
00:36:35.440 --> 00:36:39.460
D'Angelo is going to ask everyone to raise their hand if they have a vagina or if they
迪安杰洛要让所有人举手，如果他们有阴道，或者如果他们

882
00:36:39.460 --> 00:36:41.480
love someone who has a vagina.
爱着一个有阴道的人。

883
00:36:42.220 --> 00:36:43.700
Both of his hands go up.
他两只手都举了起来。

884
00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:44.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

885
00:36:44.940 --> 00:36:47.060
The scene was actually a much bigger scene.
这一幕其实原本长得多。

886
00:36:47.280 --> 00:36:48.860
And, Jenna, I thought we should hear it.
而且，珍娜，我觉得我们应该听听看。

887
00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:50.880
Angela and Phyllis speak up.
安吉拉和菲利斯站出来说话了。

888
00:36:50.980 --> 00:36:53.360
And then they also ask Toby to weigh in.
然后她们还让托比发表意见。

889
00:36:54.480 --> 00:36:57.860
Apparently, there's a rumor running around here that I'm a sexiSt.
显然，这里有个传言说我是个性别歧视者。

890
00:36:58.400 --> 00:37:01.400
D'Angelo, it's simply a question of respecting the work.
迪安杰洛，这纯粹是尊重工作的问题。

891
00:37:01.860 --> 00:37:04.560
Kevin is invited to meetings that I'm not invited to.
凯文被邀请参加的会议我却没被邀请。

892
00:37:04.720 --> 00:37:06.180
And I'm a more productive accountant.
而我是一个效率更高的会计。

893
00:37:06.360 --> 00:37:07.860
You can literally look at the numbers.
你完全可以看看数据。

894
00:37:08.180 --> 00:37:08.800
Whoa, Angela.
哇，安吉拉。

895
00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:09.760
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

896
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:12.920
It depends what makes the math dig, D'Angelo.
这取决于什么能让数学成立，迪安杰洛。

897
00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:18.880
I'm not a feminist, but I think that the men in this office are being given chances that
我不是女权主义者，但我认为办公室里的男性得到的那些机会，

898
00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:19.820
the women aren't.
女性却没有。

899
00:37:19.820 --> 00:37:21.180
Right, Toby?
对吧，托比？

900
00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:24.260
I mean, isn't there some policy on this?
我是说，难道没有关于这方面的政策吗？

901
00:37:26.340 --> 00:37:26.880
Easy.
放轻松。

902
00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:32.520
I had a difficult relationship with my last boss.
我和上一任老板的关系很僵。

903
00:37:33.520 --> 00:37:39.480
Not eager to create another hostile situation.
不想再制造什么敌对局面了。

904
00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:40.860
Whoa.
哇。

905
00:37:41.580 --> 00:37:42.080
Yeah.
是啊。

906
00:37:43.160 --> 00:37:49.580
Also, the way Paul delivers that talking head as Toby, he puts so many spaces between the
另外，保罗在演托比那段访谈时，他在词与词之间留了太多停顿，

907
00:37:49.580 --> 00:37:51.880
words that I kind of felt like Michael Scott.
让我感觉自己就像迈克尔·斯科特一样。

908
00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:53.540
I was like, say it!
我当时心想，快说啊！

909
00:37:55.060 --> 00:37:56.660
Well, we got a fan.
好吧，我们有位粉丝来信了。

910
00:37:57.220 --> 00:37:58.740
I don't know what you would call it.
我不知道该怎么称呼它。

911
00:37:58.820 --> 00:38:01.220
I'm calling it a fan soapbox from Anna W.
我把它称为来自英国安娜·W的粉丝吐槽。

912
00:38:01.400 --> 00:38:01.900
in England.
在英国。

913
00:38:02.400 --> 00:38:03.220
Oh, let's hear it.
哦，让我们听听看。

914
00:38:03.340 --> 00:38:06.360
Anna said, I've held my tongue about Phyllis long enough.
安娜说，关于菲利斯，我忍得够久了。

915
00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:09.160
Phyllis in this episode pisses me off.
这一集里的菲利斯真让我火大。

916
00:38:09.460 --> 00:38:09.720
Oh.
哦。

917
00:38:10.480 --> 00:38:14.720
Phyllis says, quote, I'm not a feminist, but I think the men in this office are being
菲利斯说，引用一下，我不是女权主义者，但我认为办公室里的男同事

918
00:38:14.720 --> 00:38:16.280
given chances that women aren't.
得到了女同事没有的机会。

919
00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:21.880
Anna says, Phyllis, that is feminism.
安娜说，菲利斯，那就是女权主义。

920
00:38:22.820 --> 00:38:28.660
Equality and opportunity, equality and pay, and rights is being a feminiSt.
平等的机遇、平等的薪酬和权利，这就是女权主义。

921
00:38:28.980 --> 00:38:31.940
You are a feminist if that's what you think, Phyllis.
如果你是这么想的，菲利斯，那你就是女权主义者。

922
00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:33.740
Thank you, Anna.
谢谢你，安娜。

923
00:38:33.740 --> 00:38:42.720
Yeah, because I'm going to say, for some reason, I feel like feminist has become like
没错，因为我想说，不知为何，我觉得女权主义者这个词

924
00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:44.780
this dirty word somehow, right?
好像变成了一个贬义词，对吧？

925
00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:45.120
Right.
没错。

926
00:38:45.120 --> 00:38:46.720
Like somehow like being a feminiSt.
就像某种程度上，成为一名女权主义者。

927
00:38:47.020 --> 00:38:47.840
It's become charged.
它变得敏感了。

928
00:38:48.100 --> 00:38:48.640
Charged.
敏感。

929
00:38:48.860 --> 00:38:48.910
Yeah.
是啊。

930
00:38:48.910 --> 00:38:50.280
It's such a good way to put it, Angela.
安吉拉，你总结得真好。

931
00:38:50.540 --> 00:38:55.600
And it shouldn't be charged if you just want equal opportunity, pay, and rights.
如果你只是想要平等的机遇、薪酬和权利，那它本不该变得敏感。

932
00:38:56.100 --> 00:38:56.280
Yeah.
没错。

933
00:38:56.280 --> 00:38:57.340
That's it.
就是这样。

934
00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:57.980
The end.
结束。

935
00:38:58.260 --> 00:38:58.520
Fair.
公平。

936
00:38:58.800 --> 00:39:01.060
Not much more complicated than that.
没那么复杂。

937
00:39:01.220 --> 00:39:02.260
Can we just get fair?
我们能得到公平吗？

938
00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:05.040
Ah, there you go.
啊，说得好。

939
00:39:05.440 --> 00:39:06.380
Thank you, Anna.
谢谢你，安娜。

940
00:39:06.560 --> 00:39:07.280
I liked that.
我喜欢这个。

941
00:39:07.460 --> 00:39:08.600
Anna, you made her day.
安娜，你让她今天过得很开心。

942
00:39:08.920 --> 00:39:09.560
You did.
确实。

943
00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:14.900
At the end of the scene, D'Angelo's new executive assistant is going to arrive.
在这一幕结束时，德安杰洛的新任行政助理就要登场了。

944
00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:18.640
I wanted to describe this character per the shooting draft.
我想根据拍摄剧本描述一下这个角色。

945
00:39:18.880 --> 00:39:19.040
Okay.
好的。

946
00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:24.340
Erin enters with a tall, gorgeous young woman, Jordan Garfield.
艾琳带着一位高挑、美艳的年轻女性乔丹·加菲尔德走了进来。

947
00:39:24.600 --> 00:39:26.520
D'Angelo shakes her hand.
德安杰洛与她握手。

948
00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.160
Jordan seems weirded out by the attention.
乔丹似乎对这种关注感到有些不自在。

949
00:39:30.020 --> 00:39:30.240
Hmm.
嗯。

950
00:39:30.740 --> 00:39:32.380
Well, new character alert.
好吧，新角色预警。

951
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:34.560
Jordan was played by Cody Horn.
乔丹由科迪·霍恩饰演。

952
00:39:34.820 --> 00:39:37.220
She has a three-episode arc on the show.
她在剧中有一个三集的戏份。

953
00:39:37.220 --> 00:39:41.900
And you might recognize her from the TV series Rescue Me or the movie Magic Mike.
你可能在电视剧《火线救援》或电影《魔力麦克》中见过她。

954
00:39:42.540 --> 00:39:49.040
When she enters, Pam is suspicious and immediately begins asking her about her previous work experience.
当她进来时，帕姆心存疑虑，立刻开始询问她之前的工作经历。

955
00:39:49.340 --> 00:39:54.000
We find out she worked at Anthropologie, and we learn that that's Kelly's dream job.
我们发现她在Anthropologie工作过，而那是凯莉梦寐以求的工作。

956
00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:57.600
I love it when she's like, you quit that job to come here?
我喜欢她那种语气，就像在说，你辞掉那份工作来这儿？

957
00:39:57.680 --> 00:40:00.640
And my thought was, Kelly, go apply.
而我的想法是，凯莉，去应聘吧。

958
00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:01.920
They'll hire you.
他们会录用你的。

959
00:40:02.100 --> 00:40:04.000
But she's like, how'd you get that job?
但她却说，你是怎么得到那份工作的？

960
00:40:04.060 --> 00:40:04.580
I know.
我知道。

961
00:40:04.580 --> 00:40:08.960
Well, we do learn that this is Jordan's first office job ever.
嗯，我们确实了解到这是乔丹的第一份办公室工作。

962
00:40:09.380 --> 00:40:09.900
Yes.
是的。

963
00:40:10.700 --> 00:40:15.180
And then the inner circle is going to gather, and Jim is no longer invited.
然后核心圈子要聚会了，吉姆不再受邀。

964
00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:16.740
He did not get a text.
他没收到短信。

965
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:20.240
Dwight got a text, but he's not interested.
德怀特收到了短信，但他不感兴趣。

966
00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:22.520
Guess who did get a text?
猜猜谁收到了短信？

967
00:40:23.100 --> 00:40:23.620
Andy.
安迪。

968
00:40:23.960 --> 00:40:25.380
And boy, has he flipped.
天哪，他彻底变了。

969
00:40:25.680 --> 00:40:26.400
I know.
我知道。

970
00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:28.320
He's so excited to run in there.
他兴奋得要命，想跑进去。

971
00:40:28.320 --> 00:40:35.120
Jim tries to go in, sort of enters, and he gets fully kicked out.
吉姆试着进去，算是进去了，结果被彻底赶了出来。

972
00:40:36.320 --> 00:40:36.840
Awkward.
尴尬。

973
